SUMMARY:Unearthing Stories of Female Artists in Exile and Resistance
DESCRIPTION:Session two of a two-part discussion series exploring the 
 graphic memoirs of the late Marjane Satrapi. In Persepolis 2\, Satrapi 
 picks up where she left off\, navigating exile in Vienna as a young woman\, 
 caught between Iranian roots and a European life\, searching for identity 
 and belonging across two worlds. Participants receive a copy of Persepolis 
 2\, available for pickup at the Main Branch. We will also enjoy Persian 
 Palmers and cookies! Part of Adult Summer Reading 2026: Unearth a 
 Story.\n\nSign up for summer reading here for children\, teens\, and 
 adults! Earn tickets for your reading and enter to win exciting prizes!
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Book Discussion
UID:LibCal-10306-17035218
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17035218
END:VEVENT
