SUMMARY:The First Birds of Autumn NEW
DESCRIPTION:Note: This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nWe will visit a different site each week to witness the 
 southbound migration of birds from as far away as Alaska and the Russian 
 Far East. Vireos\, warblers\, and tanagers are among the songbirds likely 
 to be seen in August and September\, along with a good range of wading 
 birds. Our destinations will be set shortly before each excursion\, the 
 choice determined by recent reports of concentrations of migrants. \n
LOCATION:Montclair - Offsite\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Home & Garden
