BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260827T220000Z
DTEND:20260827T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260827T000000Z
SUMMARY:Queer Lit Club
DESCRIPTION:This month we will be reading "Fruit Fly" by Josh Silver.\n\nA 
 BBC must-read book of 2026—”Sharp\, dark and humorous\, it’s a real 
 nail-biter.”\n\nGo gay. Go sad. Go dark.\n\nA washed-up author will stop 
 at nothing to claw her way back to relevancy—even if it means 
 appropriating a young gay man’s tragic story.\n\nMallory Maddox is buried 
 under seven years of writer’s block. With her status as a literary 
 sensation fizzling\, she’ll do anything she can to resurrect her career. 
 Inspiration needs to strike—and fast.\n\nEnter Leo. He’s a struggling 
 addict sleeping under bridges and trading sex for survival. He’s 
 vulnerable. He’s enigmatic. He’s exactly what Mallory has been looking 
 for. \n\nMallory needs Leo if she wants another bestseller. The world needs 
 Leo’s story right now\, and Mallory believes she deserves to tell it. 
 Really\, it’s her story—she’s the one who wrote it\, after all. 
 \n\nBut as secrets threaten to unravel more than just her career\, Mallory 
 must decide how far she will go to pen the perfect story. \n\nA razor-sharp 
 satirical thriller\, Fruit Fly will appeal to fans of R. F. Kuang’s 
 Yellowface and Yomi Adegoke’s The List.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Tower Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Book Discussion, Books, Film & Theater
UID:LibCal-10306-16654246
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16654246
END:VEVENT
