DTSTAMP:20260914T000000Z
SUMMARY:60th Anniversary of MLK in Montclair - 'King in the Wilderness' Film Screening and Discussion
DESCRIPTION:This is a free Adult School program. Please register 
 below.\n\nThe Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr\, visited Montclair High 
 School on Sept. 11\, 1966 to speak at the retirement of Rev. D.C. Rice\, 
 pastor of Union Baptist Church and an early mentor. A planned ceremony at 
 Montclair High school was met with community uproar\, leading to two 
 separate King speeches on school grounds.\n\nWe will recognize the 60th 
 anniversary of this event with a film screening of King in the Wilderness 
 (2018) by a discussion and Q&A moderated by Dr. Leslie Wilson of Montclair 
 State University.\n\n"King in the Wilderness offers a window into the final 
 years of the civil rights icon's life after the signing of the Voting Right 
 Acts of 1965 and amid an American landscape divided by the Vietnam War and 
 tensions over race and poverty. King's unwavering commitment to nonviolence 
 and compassion shines through in archived footage and the stories of those 
 who were around him."\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Lectures / History & Culture
UID:LibCal-10306-16803076
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16803076
END:VEVENT
