SUMMARY:Understanding Medicare
DESCRIPTION:Confused about Medicare? Join us for an informative session 
 that breaks down the basics of this federal health insurance program. Learn 
 who qualifies\, including adults age 65 and older\, younger individuals 
 with disabilities\, and those with End-Stage Renal Disease 
 (ESRD).\n\nWe’ll explain the different parts of Medicare—Part A 
 (hospital insurance)\, Part B (medical insurance)\, and Part D 
 (prescription drug coverage)—and what services each covers. The program 
 will also explore your coverage options\, including Original Medicare with 
 supplemental (Medigap) plans and Medicare Advantage (Part C).\n\nThis 
 session is ideal for anyone approaching Medicare eligibility\, caregivers\, 
 or those looking to better understand their health coverage 
 choices.\n\nPresented by Medicare Specialist Jacki Spear.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Finances
