SUMMARY:Stronger Montclair: An Introduction to the Strong Towns Movement
DESCRIPTION:What does it take to make Montclair a great place to live while 
 remaining financially sustainable?\n\nJoin us for an introduction to the 
 Strong Towns movement and explore how its ideas can help Montclair build a 
 stronger\, more resilient future. We’ll examine the challenges of 
 suburban development\, municipal finances\, housing\, transportation\, 
 parking\, and land use—and discuss practical principles for creating a 
 prosperous community at a human scale.\n\nThe program will conclude with a 
 discussion of next steps for Montclair residents and how we can work 
 together to build a stronger town.\n\nCome learn\, ask questions\, and 
 explore what Strong Towns could mean for Montclair.\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Meeting
