DTSTAMP:20260924T000000Z
SUMMARY:'The Shoes' Play Reading
DESCRIPTION:Come enjoy a reading of The Shoes before it hits the New York 
 Winter Festival (NYWinterfest) this year!\n\n\nThe Shoes follows the story 
 of Kent Warner\, the man who changed the course of Hollywood history when 
 he discovered Judy Garland's iconic ruby slippers from The Wizard of Oz 
 hidden away in storage. Yet\, behind the glitz and glamour of showbiz\, 
 Kent struggled with his identity\, a sense of belonging\, and the search 
 for love—often using his passion for classic cinema to escape his own 
 reality.\n\nIn a world of good and bad witches\, of empty heads and aching 
 hearts\, Kent ultimately proved to be the courage at the center of it all.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Books, Film & Theater
UID:LibCal-10306-15852712
