SUMMARY:Celebrate the publication Shibu's New Friend with author Tess Thomas (recommended for ages 4-8)
DESCRIPTION:Join author Tess Thomas for a special storytime at the 
 Montclair Public Library! Tess will read her debut picture book\, SHIBU'S 
 TAIL\, as well as her brand-new sequel\, SHIBU'S NEW FRIEND. The books 
 follow the adventures of a cat named Shibu\, who has big feelings and an 
 even bigger tail. SHIBU'S TAIL has earned four starred reviews\, multiple 
 best-of-year lists\, and has been published in over 18 different countries. 
 Following the readings\, Tess will answer questions from the audience and 
 lead young readers in a Shibu and Dottie-themed craft. Copies of SHIBU'S 
 TAIL and SHIBU'S NEW FRIEND will be available for purchase and signing 
 following the event.\n\nRegistration is recommended but not required.\n\n 
 \n\n\n\nTess Thomas is a writer living in Hoboken\, New Jersey. She started 
 her storytelling career at the age of four\, when she would dictate tales 
 about her imaginary friends\, Sami the cat and Doodie the dog\, and send 
 them to her grandparents. Her first book\, SHIBU'S TAIL\, earned four 
 starred reviews\, multiple best-of-year lists\, and has been published in 
 over a dozen different languages. Tess’ favorite part of being an author 
 is visiting schools\, libraries\, and bookstores to connect with young 
 readers. She loves french fries\, her kids\, and her husband (sometimes in 
 that order).\n\nSHIBU'S NEW FRIEND\n\nShibu and Dottie are as different as 
 cats and dogs — but maybe they have more in common than they think in 
 this charming sequel to the international hit SHIBU'S TAIL!\n\nShibu has a 
 lot of friends and they have a lot in common. It’s a lot of fun! But then 
 comes … Dottie. Dottie is a DOG and she does things a bit differently. 
 She barks instead of purrs. She tears up boxes instead of sitting inside 
 them. She spends a lot of time … digging?\n\nShibu isn’t sure about a 
 new friend\, especially one so different\, but he can’t help feeling like 
 Dottie’s love for life is a lot like his own. Could this new friend 
 actually become his best pal? Published by Levine Querido\, SHIBU'S NEW 
 FRIEND hits shelves on September 1\, 2026!\n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Green Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Author Talk, Children's Programs
UID:LibCal-10306-17029924
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17029924
END:VEVENT
