BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261020T171500Z
DTEND:20261020T181500Z
DTSTAMP:20261020T000000Z
SUMMARY:Everything Book Club\, "Kin" by Tayari Jones\, Session 2
DESCRIPTION:An instant New York Times bestseller by the author of "An 
 American Marriage." A selection for both Oprah's Book Club and The New York 
 Times Book Review Book Club. \n\nGoes with the Open Book / Open Mind 
 program with Tayari Jones about "Kin" the following week on Tuesday\, 
 September 15! Tickets cost $35 and include a signed copy of the book. (If 
 for any reason you can't afford a ticket\, come talk to me.)\n\nWe'll talk 
 about Jones's conversation as well as "Kin\," a poignant historical novel 
 set in the civil rights era about two motherless childhood friends who take 
 very different journeys: one to the storied HBCU Spellman College\, the 
 other to make her way in the world. \n\nTAYARI JONES is the author of four 
 other novels\, most recently the New York Times bestseller "An American 
 Marriage\," which was an Oprah’s Book Club selection and also appeared on 
 Barack Obama’s summer reading list and his year-end roundup. It won the 
 Women’s Prize for Fiction\, the Aspen Words Literary Prize\, and an NAACP 
 Image Award and has been published in two dozen countries. Jones is the 
 C.H. Candler Professor of English and Creative Writing at Emory University 
 and lives in Atlanta.\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Book Discussion
UID:LibCal-10306-17281067
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17281067
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261020T193000Z
DTEND:20261020T201500Z
DTSTAMP:20261020T000000Z
SUMMARY:Tech Talks
DESCRIPTION:Tech Talks is a free informational series where library staff 
 introduce and explain the technology topics that matter most in today's 
 digital world. Each session takes a closer look at a new or complex 
 topic—whether it's a trending app\, an emerging technology\, or a 
 platform you've been hearing about but aren't quite sure how to navigate. 
 Through demonstrations and clear\, jargon-free explanations\, you'll come 
 away with a better understanding of the tech landscape around you. There's 
 no hands-on component\, so no devices are needed—just come ready to learn 
 and ask questions.\n\nAll are welcome regardless of experience level\, and 
 time is reserved at the end of each session for Q&A. Sessions are free and 
 open to the public.\n\nThis week's topic is: TBD
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Classroom
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Computers & Technology
UID:LibCal-10306-16825385
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16825385
